<p>ConsumedCapacity -&gt; (list)</p>
<blockquote>
<div><p>The capacity units consumed by the entire <code class="docutils literal notranslate"><span class="pre">BatchWriteItem</span></code> operation.</p>
<p>Each element consists of:</p>
<ul class="simple">
<li><code class="docutils literal notranslate"><span class="pre">TableName</span></code> - The table that consumed the provisioned throughput.</li>
<li><code class="docutils literal notranslate"><span class="pre">CapacityUnits</span></code> - The total number of capacity units consumed.</li>
</ul>
<p>If the table has vector indexes, each element also includes a <code class="docutils literal notranslate"><span class="pre">VectorIndexes</span></code> field with <code class="docutils literal notranslate"><span class="pre">VectorWriteRequestBytes</span></code> consumed for each affected vector index.</p>
<p>(structure)</p>
<blockquote>
<div><p>The capacity units consumed by an operation. The data returned includes the total provisioned throughput consumed, along with statistics for the table and any indexes involved in the operation. <code class="docutils literal notranslate"><span class="pre">ConsumedCapacity</span></code> is only returned if the request asked for it. For more information, see <a class="reference external" href="https://docs.aws.amazon.com/amazondynamodb/latest/developerguide/provisioned-capacity-mode.html">Provisioned capacity mode</a> in the <em>Amazon DynamoDB Developer Guide</em> .</p>
<p>TableName -&gt; (string)</p>
<blockquote>
